## 4.3.0 (2026-09-07)

Selection replacement, and a clipboard bug that has been in this app since it
was pot.

### New:

-   **Selection replacement.** A hotkey that translates whatever you have selected and types the translation back over it, without a window ever appearing. Bind it under Settings → Hotkey; it is unbound by default. Windows only for now — macOS needs its accessibility permission behind a synthesised Cmd+V, and on Linux the answer depends on the session, since Wayland gives no application a sanctioned way to synthesise input into another

### Bugs fixed:

-   **selection translate no longer destroys your clipboard.** Reading the selection borrows the clipboard, and putting it back only ever restored one flavour of what was there: HTML copied from a browser came back as plain text, RTF from a word processor lost its formatting, and a copied file list vanished outright. Every format is now saved and restored, including the private ones applications use to paste back into themselves losslessly. Images survive too, as long as the source offered a DIB — which almost all of them do
-   the translate window took focus even in the modes that keep it hidden, because it was focused a moment before anything had decided whether to show it

### Internal:

-   the text to translate and how the translation started are now written together, so a mode cannot outlive the request that set it
